Part 1a: dA/(dtheta dphi) = sin(2*theta)/2 = cos(theta) * [sin(theta) dtheta dphi = dOmega]
         density on the hemisphere = cos(theta)/pi; total mass = 1
Part 1b: boundary equation minus ellipse x1^2/cos^2(alpha) + x2^2 = 1 : 0
         P(+ | u, n) = [area of disk minus (left half-disk minus left half-ellipse)]/pi = cos(alpha)/2 + 1/2
Part 2: finite disk grids, u = X+, n = R (cos alpha = 4/5): target 9/10
   M=  5:    80 cells, P = 9/10, error = 0
   M= 20:  1264 cells, P = 71/79, error = 1/790
   M= 80: 20108 cells, P = 9049/10054, error = 1/25135
Part 3: conditional swap on the M=5 grid is injective: True ( 12800 images )
        the system after outcome sigma is the lift of a fresh uniform seed around sigma*n, independent of
        the old lambda, which sits in the dump register: the KS update rule realized by a bijection,
        at the cost of one fresh disk seed per measurement and an inaccessible dump.
